(a) General handling requirements. No person shall engage in solid waste handling in a manner which will:
(1) Be conducive to insect and rodent infestation or the harboring and feeding of wild dogs or other animals;
(2) Impair the air quality;
(3) Impair the quality of the ground or surface waters;
(4) Impair the quality of the environment; or
(5) Create other hazards to the public health, safety or well-being.
(b) Application of article. The provisions of this article apply to all persons presently engaged in solid waste handling as well as all persons to engage in solid waste handling in the future.
(Ord. of 2-21-1998, § 2)
